 ## rates
 
 - `rates.quote(weight_kg, zone)`: price for a weight and zone
+
+## returns
+
+- `returns.request_return(shipment_id, reason)`: file a return request for a delivered shipment, stamped with `requested_at`; emits `return.requested`. Not idempotent: each call files a new request, up to `settings.MAX_RETURNS_PER_SHIPMENT` (3) per shipment
+  - `E_NOT_FOUND`: the shipment does not exist
+  - `E_BAD_INPUT`: the reason is empty or not a string
+  - `E_BAD_STATE`: the shipment is not delivered (detail is its current status)
+  - `E_LIMIT`: the shipment already has 3 return requests
+- `returns.returns_for(shipment_id)`: return requests filed for a shipment, sorted by id; `[]` when there are none (read-only)
+  - `E_NOT_FOUND`: the shipment does not exist
